    <bugTrackerUrl>https://whatpulse.org/help/</bugTrackerUrl>
    <tags>whatpulse productivity statistics tracking keyboard mouse network usage</tags>
    <summary>Analyze your productivity and activity using WhatPulse.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
WhatPulse measures your computer activity: keyboard and mouse usage, time spent in applications, network traffic, and uptime. It runs quietly in the background and turns that data into statistics you can explore locally or on [whatpulse.org](https://whatpulse.org/).

## Notes

- Installs machine-wide (`InstallForAllUsers=true`) into `%ProgramFiles%\WhatPulse`.
- Npcap is installed alongside WhatPulse for network statistics (the installer's default).
- Upgrades run the new installer over the existing installation; settings and local data are kept.
- Uninstalling runs `WhatPulseMaintenanceTool.exe purge`, which removes the program directory.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://whatpulse.org/releasenotes/{{VERSION}}</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>